@startuml
title Sequence diagram: coordinator rejects an event during planning
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' The coordinator works in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login
' token, so the call and its answer are two arrows each: person <-> Web App, then
' Web App <-> the Backend API. This page looks inside the Backend API, so its
' modules are lifelines. Only the arrows between the Web App, the modules and
' PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the draw.io and PDF versions.
' It is a modular monolith: an arrow between two modules is a call to the other
' module's service function, in the same process (no network hop). The status change,
' the releases and the returned equipment share one database session and are saved in
' one commit; the notifications are saved after it, written by the notifications
' module. A notification is only a record in PostgreSQL: nothing is pushed to its
' recipient, who fetches it later (see the who-is-told page).

actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "events\nmodule" as events
participant "venue\nmodule" as venue
participant "notifications\nmodule" as notifications
participant "equipment\nmodule" as equipment
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Reject an event during planning (it must be Approved or in Safety Review; a reason is required) ==
coordinator -> web : Reject, with a reason
autonumber
web -> events : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/reject
events -> db : Check: Approved or in Safety Review,\nno pending change request
group Saved together, in one commit
  events -> db : Status becomes rejected, add\ndecision entry (with the reason)
  events -> venue : release_event_arrangements
  venue -> db : Withdraw pending, conflicting,\nrejected or expired requests
  venue -> db : Release approved and on_hold\nrequests, cancel their bookings
  events -> equipment : release_event_reservations
  equipment -> db : Return reserved equipment
end

== After the commit: the notifications are saved ==
events -> notifications : notify_users\n(the organiser, with the reason)
notifications -> db : Save notification: organiser,\nwith the reason
events -> venue : tell_venue_staff_of_releases
venue -> notifications : notify_users,\nonce per release
notifications -> db : Save one booking_released notice\nper release, for every Venue Staff user
events --> web : The request, now rejected
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the request
@enduml
